{"notes": "The panel reveals a disinflationary backdrop meeting moderately loose financial conditions, with labour tightening at the margin but from a base already near full employment. Inflation has rolled over sharply: headline has fallen nearly 1.2pp in the last three months, from 2.44% to 1.64%, while core PCE sits at 1.55%, well below the Fed's 2% target and below headline. The 3-month annualized core rate stands at just 0.98%, a benign level. Inflation expectations remain anchored; the 10-year breakeven sits at 1.73%, in the lower half of its 12-month range and 27bp below the 2% target. This backdrop supports lower nominal yields on a duration basis.

